 "note": "Template registry — the routing brain (Plan §22-23). Maps a user request to the right slide construction. Each template: the family/subfamily it serves, the layout pattern(s) to use, required + optional inputs, when to use / when to avoid, canonical source slide, and a fallback. The designer reads this to decide HOW Kumulus normally makes a given slide. Pair with selection-rules.md. | G4: each template now points to a built Phase-B skeleton (components/structures/*); requiredInputs are the facts the skeleton's slots need.",
